Let $S_k$ be the sum of weights of the boxes in the $k$-th block of size $k$.
The boxes are partitioned into blocks of size $k$:
Block 1: indices $1$ to $k$. Sum $B_1 = \sum_{i=1}^k a_i$.
Block 2: indices $k+1$ to $2k$. Sum $B_2 = \sum_{i=k+1}^{2k} a_i$.
...
Block $m$: indices $(m-1)k+1$ to $mk$. Sum $B_m = \sum_{i=(m-1)k+1}^{mk} a_i$, where $m = n/k$.

For a fixed $k$, we want to find $\max_{1 \le i \le m} B_i - \min_{1 \le j \le m} B_j$.
